Z||000010||1FST2M6||03-24-2000||01:40 PM||||MW - I realize that IF i had done somthing out of the norm or had some one run a light or the Taco Bell sign would have fallen on my car I would be ultimately held responcible. Sorry for the sarcasim. (sp) <BR>I just left a message for her.. I'll post thier web site... "Girlie Girl" we've Been together for 2 years now, I got her started in the Sport and haven't ever forced her to do ANYTHING she didn't want to. loves to run at Commerce and likes to pick on guys... "you got beat by a GIRL in a SATURN..!" heard her tell kids that a few times.  Not so sure about anyone being any different here, He's from Minn, and just moved a few weeks ago to Billings, Montana... He just says the same as I do.. why have a toy if you can't play with it.  I'll get a Pic of his car.. Really sweet! He won't let me drive it.. suprise suprise... <BR>Geez Chad...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> you've been there too hunh..   <BR>Dan - A buddy of Mine has a Kart. Dirt track 3/4" off the ground 60+mph. I'd like at least a fighting chance to live if I ever lose it. Probly not as dangerous as it looks but You've got more guts than I.   <BR>Moo - You driven a SE/GT V6 after driving a CRX? their 1.6 doesn't hold a candle to the Fieros Torque and Traction! ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Dan86gt3.8||03-24-2000||02:02 PM||||Hey karting is actually pretty safe.  I don't even know if anybody has ever even died doing it.  And yes it is scary as hell.  You defenitely have to start slow and work your way up.  and soon you will find your self pushing it harder in ther corners and mixing it up with guy next to you.  If you never push yourself, you will never get faster.  Ohhh by the way I race sprint (asphalt track) on a marhgay chassis with a 135 bm reed valve on a horstman axle clutch.  It feels 3 times faster and pulss 5 timnes as hard in the corners as the fiero does.  Its a rush, I recomend everyone try it!!!!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||6
Z||000012||1FST2M6||03-24-2000||03:53 PM||||i'll get in touch with my frined and bug him about what he has.. all i know is it's got REALLY expensive tiny tires.. $100 each for a 4"ish tire guess there about 7-8" wide.. a 5hp briggs looking block, COOL hand held starter, a shiney billet head, an intake assembly as long as my arm, offset motor and seat, Red tube chassis and Red Fiberglas.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> sorry i'm so uninformed. I'm sure it's safe.. racing suit, helmet and neck brace is his uniform.. and I have't seen any one really get hurt at all... trash their 'glas or mess with the tires and kart but no ambulance.. that i've seen ... I've only been about 4 weekends... I'll find out what all he has.. He can pull over a g on a skid pad with out trying...! HOW COOL IS THAT! He spent less on his toy than I did on my Fiero and it's actually cooler! .. not street legal but SWEET! too bad he's only "Go Fast Turn Left" ||||reg||1
